            <ArticleTitle>Low-dose subcutaneous ketamine infusion and morphine tolerance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>101-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The NMDA receptor has been reported to be involved in opioid tolerance. Adjuvant subcutaneous infusion treatment with (very) low-dose ketamine, a NMDA receptor antagonist, improves analgesia and at the same time appears to reduce morphine tolerance. Three cases are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
